{
 "comment": "Half-rack LXP-1. The front panel has three analogue pots (INPUT/MIX/OUTPUT, not in MIDI), a 16-position Program selector and two parameter knobs, DECAY (param 0) and DELAY (param 1), whose meaning depends on the running algorithm (Program ID). Rows follow that panel: program (algorithm + effects level, the one param every algorithm shares), then one group per algorithm family with its DECAY and DELAY knobs first and the SysEx-only params after them, then the Dynamic MIDI patches and the live/system params (input level is reset to max on every recall; setup number = the Program knob, 128-143 = presets). Params 0-9 share wire numbers across algorithms, so only the group matching the current Program ID is live; the others are dimmed by meaning, not by the editor. Patch offsets (read-only) are not shown; the name is edited in the name field (name1-16).",
